        {'t': 'p', 'text': 'The census says about 73 percent of occupied homes in Santa Monica are renter-occupied. Whether you rent or own, the rules for who handles repairs differ. If you rent, tell your landlord or association right away, and ask who handles the appliance, the flooring and the repair.'},
        {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Stacked layouts make a leak a shared problem, whether the building is in [Santa Monica](/service-area/santa-monica-ca/), in [Playa Vista](/service-area/playa-vista-ca/) or around the Marina Del Rey basins, because water that leaves one home tends to reach the ceiling or wall of another. The people next door deserve an early warning.'},
        {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Under-floor travel is the part people miss. Water that leaves a laundry closet or kitchen can slide along the subfloor beneath cabinets and walls, then sit in places a mop never reaches. A crew follows the readings, not the visible puddle, which is why the wet area is often larger than it looks.'},
        {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Ice makers deserve a mention too. A refrigerator line can drip behind the unit for weeks with no visible puddle. By the time a floor warps or a smell shows up, the underlayment may be saturated. Pull the refrigerator out gently and look at the wall and floor before assuming the damp spot is a one-time spill.'},
        {'t': 'p', 'text': 'Dishwashers fail differently. A cracked drain hose or a loose inlet fitting leaks only while the cycle runs, so the damage builds in short bursts under the cabinet. If you see a damp toe kick or a dark stain on the floor near the unit, shut the supply valve and have the area checked with a meter before the next load.'},
        {'t': 'h2', 'text': 'What changes the scope and cost'},
